Every account gets 2G of disk (with a little room over that for a
while), 1G of RAM, 200 processes and one CPU.

  quota -s      disk used and the limit
  du -sh ~/*    what's taking the space

When a program runs out of memory it gets killed, and when you hit the
process limit new ones won't start. Nothing is wrong with the server
when that happens, it's the limit.
